.TH "OPS\-EXEC" 1 "" "ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ops\-exec \- run a command
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBops exec\fR <argv...>
.PP
Every word after \fBexec\fR is passed through as written, so options go before
\fBexec\fR.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fI<argv...>\fR
the command and its arguments
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
say more (repeatable)
.br
repeat to count: \-vvv
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIstring\fR
when to color (default auto) [auto|always|never]
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBops\fR(1)
